---
/**
 * Terms of Use for the website. Programme terms (fees, refunds, instalments)
 * stay in BIA's official documents and on /fees — this page does not restate
 * or change them. Approved by BIA (November 2026).
 */
import DocPage from '../components/DocPage.astro';
import { adsEnabled } from '../data/ads';
import { cbt, email, office, primaryContact, site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '2026-11-13';
---

<DocPage
  title="Terms of Use | BIA JUPEB — Boma’s Intellectual Academy"
  description="Terms for using biajupeb.com.ng, the website of BIA JUPEB (Boma’s Intellectual Academy): information accuracy, content ownership, links and advertising."
  eyebrow="Terms"
  heading="Terms of Use"
  lead="The terms that apply when you use biajupeb.com.ng. Please read them together with our Privacy Policy."
  updated={updated}
>
  <h2>About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    This website is run by {site.parent} (“BIA”, “we”, “us”). By using it you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please
    do not use the website.
  </p>

  <h2>Information on this website</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the information on this website accurate and up to date. Fees, dates, timetables and programme details can
    change, so please confirm them with the BIA admissions office before you register or make a payment. If anything on this
    website differs from BIA’s official documents or what the admissions office tells you, the official information applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    The guides on this website are general information to help you understand JUPEB and Direct Entry. Always check admission
    requirements with JUPEB and with the university you are applying to.
  </p>

  <h2>Registration and payments</h2>
  <p>
    Registration is handled by the BIA admissions office. This website does not take registrations or payments. Programme fees,
    instalments and payment terms are set out on the <a href="/fees">fees page</a> and in BIA’s official payment documents.
  </p>

  <h2>Results and testimonials</h2>
  <p>
    Student results on this website come from BIA’s records; students are named or pictured only where BIA has confirmed their
    permission. Results show what individual students achieved; they are not a promise that every student will get the same
    result.
  </p>

  <h2>Content and trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    The text, photographs, videos, logos and design of this website belong to BIA or are used with permission. You may view and
    share links to our pages, and print pages for personal use. Please do not copy, republish or sell our content, or use the BIA
    name or logo, without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the website</h2>
  <p>
    Please do not misuse the website — for example by trying to gain unauthorised access, disrupting how it works, or using
    automated tools to copy its content.
  </p>

  <h2>Links and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This website links to other services, such as WhatsApp, Facebook, TikTok, Google Maps and BIA’s CBT practice platform at
    {' '}{cbt.host}, which have their own terms.
    {adsEnabled
      ? ' This website also shows advertisements served by Google AdSense.'
      : ' In future this website may also show advertisements served by Google AdSense.'}
    {' '}Advertisements are labelled, are chosen by the advertising service rather than by BIA, and do not mean BIA endorses the
    advertiser.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We provide this website as it is and cannot guarantee it will always be available or free of errors. As far as the law
    allows, BIA is not responsible for loss caused by relying on information on this website without confirming it with the
    admissions office, or by your use of other websites linked from it.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The “Last updated” date above shows when they last changed.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <address>
    <strong>{site.parent}</strong><br />
    {office.name}<br />
    {office.lines.map((l) => <>{l}<br /></>)}
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${primaryContact.phone}`}>{primaryContact.display}</a><br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
  </address>
</DocPage>
